-- title:
--   Primes of the j-chart of X₁(Mp) are conjugate over the floor
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M \ge 5$ with $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $\{p\}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K$ and $K_1$ be intermediate fields of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ with $K$ the subfield generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) (the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the ratios of integral forms for $\Gamma_1(Mp)$) and $K_1$ the corresponding subfield attached to $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$, and assume $K_1 \le K$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as fraction field, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $A$-algebra structures on $K$ and $K_1$ compatible with that of $L$, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j \in K$ and $j_1 \in K_1$ be nonzero elements whose underlying Laurent series are both the image of the $q$-expansion $j(q)$ under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Write $\mathcal{O} =$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and likewise $\mathcal{O}_1 =$ `chartAlgFin A K₁ j₁`, and let $\iota_F : \mathcal{O}_1 \to \mathcal{O}$ be an $A$-algebra map inducing the identity on underlying Laurent series. Then for any two points $y, y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} \mathcal{O}$ whose prime ideals have equal contractions along $\iota_F$, there is an $A$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $\mathcal{O}$ fixing $\iota_F(r)$ for every $r \in \mathcal{O}_1$ and satisfying $y' = \tau^{-1}(y)$, i.e. the prime of $y'$ is the contraction of the prime of $y$ along $\tau$.
--
--   This is the transitivity statement for the action of the relative Galois group (generated by diamond operators) on the primes of the $j$-finite chart of the integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ lying over a fixed prime of the corresponding chart for $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$. It supplies one of the inputs to [`ModularCurve.XOneP.eq_of_comap_eq_and_forall_exists_sub_mem_of_map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.eq_of_comap_eq_and_forall_exists_sub_mem_of_map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul).
